@host = http://localhost:5080
@adminToken = paste-admin-jwt
@customerToken = paste-customer-jwt

### Register a customer. The role field is ignored; the account is always a Customer.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "Password123",
  "role": "Admin"
}

### Login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### Current customer
GET {{host}}/api/customers/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Create a product (admin). Inventory is an absolute starting quantity.
POST {{host}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mechanical keyboard",
  "description": "Compact keyboard",
  "price": 79.90,
  "availableQuantity": 10
}

### List products
GET {{host}}/api/products?page=1&pageSize=20&search=key&sortBy=name&sortDirection=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Set an absolute available quantity. Version must match the last read.
PATCH {{host}}/api/products/1/inventory
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "availableQuantity": 12,
  "version": 0
}

### Place an order. Prices, totals, customer, and status are calculated by the server.
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "productId": 1, "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### Confirm, ship, or cancel
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/1/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/1/ship
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
PATCH {{host}}/api/orders/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
